WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
JAMIE: Intel's Ohio plant would like a
word.

00:00:02.625 --> 00:00:03.270
RUFUS: Precisely.

00:00:03.483 --> 00:00:06.943
ALEX: So what's the point of the
presidential visit? Just optics?

00:00:07.028 --> 00:00:10.602
JAMIE: I don't think it's only optics.
There's something real in the signal.

00:00:10.602 --> 00:00:14.176
JAMIE: The president showing up says,
with his physical presence, that this is

00:00:14.176 --> 00:00:17.749
JAMIE: a national priority. That changes
how suppliers, engineers, and states
compete for

00:00:17.749 --> 00:00:21.323
JAMIE: the downstream contracts.

00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:25.117
RUFUS: And from a capital-allocation
standpoint, two hundred and sixty-five
billion dollars anchoring

00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:28.800
RUFUS: in the United States reshapes the
geography of the global semiconductor
industry

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.484
RUFUS: over twenty years. That's not
trivial, even if it doesn't fix the

00:00:32.484 --> 00:00:36.168
RUFUS: GPU shortage in Q1.
